The team inspects what this routine produces one step at a time:
function makeCounter() {
  let n = 4000;
  return () => ++n;
}
const next = makeCounter();
next();
console.log(next());
What value is logged by the second call?

A diagnostic script executes these statements one step at a time:
const obj = { v: 4001, get() { return this.v; } };
const fn = obj.get;
console.log(fn.call(obj));
On this input, what value does the log show?

A lesson demonstrates the behavior of this code one step at a time:
function label(x = 4002) { return x; }
console.log(label());
From this trace, what is printed when no argument is passed?

A mentor asks a learner to evaluate this code:
const n = 4003;
console.log(n == '4003');
In this run, explain what this code prints and why that value follows from the language rules.
